# ouroboros#182: under-applying a compiled function BY NAME. The VM binds
# null to every unsupplied parameter; the AOT used to emit the call with too
# few arguments and leak gcc's "too few arguments" with no AOT: line. Now a
# never-read parameter takes a dummy on its C type (the #69 rule per slot),
# and a READ typed parameter refuses by name (refuse/underapplied_typed_param
# and refuse/underapplied_null_guarded). The last call has a call inside its
# argument list, so the padded slot rides the hoisted (hazard) form too.
define dead(a, b) as:
    return a * 2
print of (dead of [21])
define dead3(a, b, c) as:
    return a + b
print of (dead3 of [1, 2])
print of (dead3 of [(dead of [1]), 2])
